@startuml
title COLORS - Use Case Diagram
left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam dpi 160
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActorBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActorFontColor #222222
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor #F2F6FC
skinparam UsecaseBorderColor #333333
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #333333
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam LegendBorderColor #AAAAAA

actor User

rectangle "COLORS Web Application" {
  usecase "Log In" as Login
  usecase "Add Color" as Add
  usecase "Search Colors" as Search
  usecase "Log Out" as Logout
}

User -- Login
User -- Add
User -- Search
User -- Logout

legend bottom left
  Precondition for Add Color, Search Colors, and Log Out is that the user must be logged in.
  Add Color and Search Colors are associated with the current user ID.
endlegend

' Source verification:
' index.html invokes doLogin() in js/code.js, which posts to LAMPAPI/Login.php.
' color.html invokes addColor(), searchColor(), and doLogout() in js/code.js.
' LAMPAPI/AddColor.php inserts a color with the supplied userId.
' LAMPAPI/SearchColors.php filters color names by search text and userId.
' doLogout() clears the client identity and cookie and returns to index.html.
' Login is a prerequisite in the normal browser flow, not an included subtask
' of each add/search request. The PHP endpoints do not reauthenticate the user.
' No registration, editing, deletion, or separate view-all use case is implemented.
@enduml
